    "q-215502": {
      "dom_id": "step-q215502",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n8-|4x+5|=1.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|4x+5|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $8$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-|4x+5|=1 \\\\ 8-|4x+5|-8=1-8 \\\\ -|4x+5|=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|4x+5| & =-7 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|4x+5|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-7) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|4x+5|) & =7 \\\\ |4x+5| & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
