      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n2-|x+2|=-7.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|x+2|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $2$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-|x+2|=-7 \\\\ 2-|x+2|-2=-7-2 \\\\ -|x+2|=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|x+2| & =-9 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|x+2|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-9) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|x+2|) & =9 \\\\ |x+2| & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
