    "q-154635": {
      "dom_id": "step-q154635",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n5-|x-3|=-3.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$$\n|x-3|=k\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $5$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-|x-3|=-3 \\\\ 5-|x-3|-5=-3-5 \\\\ -|x-3|=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|x-3| & =-8 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|x-3|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|x-3|) & =8 \\\\ |x-3| & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=8.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
