/mo></mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\nSince the right-hand side is <em>negative</em>, this equation has <em>no</em> solution.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Equation III <em>has no solution</em>. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is <em>negative</em>. </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the answer is \"II and III only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
