    "q-75892": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75892",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "If $2|5x-3|+1=15,$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|5x-3|+1 & =15 \\\\ 2|5x-3| & =14 \\\\ |5x-3| & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|5x-3|=5x-3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-3| & =7 \\\\ 5x-3 & =7 \\\\ 5x & =10 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5x-3|=-(5x-3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-3| & =7 \\\\ -(5x-3) & =7 \\\\ -5x+3 & =7 \\\\ -5x & =4 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{4}{5}$ and $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
